### Sample requests for po-service (run with cds watch on port 4004)
### Sample data only.

### 1. All POs
GET http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/po/PurchaseOrders

### 2. Late POs (filter on two fields; isLate cannot be filtered because it is virtual)
GET http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/po/PurchaseOrders?$filter=dueDate%20lt%202026-11-03%20and%20deliveredQty%20lt%20orderedQty&$expand=vendor

### 3. POs sorted by due date
GET http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/po/PurchaseOrders?$orderby=dueDate

### 4. POs with their vendor
GET http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/po/PurchaseOrders?$expand=vendor

### 5. Create a PO with amount 0 (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/po/PurchaseOrders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "poNumber": "4500098",
  "vendor_ID": "V001",
  "dueDate": "2026-12-15",
  "orderedQty": 10,
  "deliveredQty": 0,
  "amount": 0
}

### 6. Create a valid PO (expect 201). Run once; a second run gives 409 because the key exists.
POST http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/po/PurchaseOrders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "poNumber": "4500099",
  "vendor_ID": "V002",
  "dueDate": "2026-12-15",
  "orderedQty": 10,
  "deliveredQty": 0,
  "amount": 15000.00
}

### 7. Valid quantities (ordered 10, delivered 5; expect 201). Run once; a second run gives 409 because the key exists.
POST http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/po/PurchaseOrders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "poNumber": "4500101",
  "vendor_ID": "V001",
  "dueDate": "2026-12-15",
  "orderedQty": 10,
  "deliveredQty": 5,
  "amount": 1000.00
}

### 8. Negative orderedQty (expect 400: "Ordered quantity must not be negative.")
POST http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/po/PurchaseOrders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "poNumber": "4500102",
  "vendor_ID": "V001",
  "dueDate": "2026-12-15",
  "orderedQty": -1,
  "deliveredQty": 0,
  "amount": 1000.00
}

### 9. Negative deliveredQty (expect 400: "Delivered quantity must not be negative.")
POST http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/po/PurchaseOrders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "poNumber": "4500103",
  "vendor_ID": "V001",
  "dueDate": "2026-12-15",
  "orderedQty": 10,
  "deliveredQty": -1,
  "amount": 1000.00
}

### 10. deliveredQty greater than orderedQty (expect 400: "Delivered quantity must not exceed ordered quantity.")
POST http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/po/PurchaseOrders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "poNumber": "4500104",
  "vendor_ID": "V001",
  "dueDate": "2026-12-15",
  "orderedQty": 10,
  "deliveredQty": 11,
  "amount": 1000.00
}
